    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dfef124b-56e9-5461-8518-a1d72c013121",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-\\frac{6}{x^{6}}+6x^{7}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{4}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{6}{x^{6}}+6x^{7}-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{4}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-6x^{-6}+6x^{7}-6x^{\\frac{-4}{3}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+6\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{\\frac{-4}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{x^{7+1}}{(7+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-4}{3}+1}}{(\\frac{-4}{3}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{6}{5x^{5}}+\\frac{3x^{8}}{4}+\\frac{18}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
