      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{6}{x^{6}}+6x^{7}-6\\sqrt[5]{x^{4}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-6x^{-6}+6x^{7}-6x^{\\frac{4}{5}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+6\\int x^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{\\frac{4}{5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{x^{7+1}}{(7+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad -6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{4}{5}+1}}{(\\frac{4}{5}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{6}{5x^{5}}+\\frac{3x^{8}}{4}-\\frac{10\\sqrt[5]{x^{9}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
